{"name":"Betta Fish","hex":"#3a6b66","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"betta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any fish of the genus Betta, especially Betta splendens (the Siamese fighting fish)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pronunciation spelling of better, comparative of good."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/betta"},{"term":"fish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A typically cold-blooded vertebrate animal that lives in water, moving with the help of fins and breathing with gills; any vertebrate that is not a tetrapod.","Any vertebrate, including tetrapods."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A period of time spent fishing.","An instance of seeking something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Betta","blocks":[{"text":"Betta is a large genus of small, active, often colorful, freshwater ray-finned fishes, in the gourami family (Osphronemidae). The best known Betta species is B. splendens, commonly known as the Siamese fighting fish and often kept as an aquarium pet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Betta_albimarginata_060311_8.jpg/330px-Betta_albimarginata_060311_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betta"},{"title":"Fish","blocks":[{"text":"A fish is an aquatic, anamniotic, gill-bearing vertebrate animal with a tough cranium to protect the brain, but lacking limbs with digits. Fish can be grouped into the more basal jawless fish and the more common jawed fish, the latter including all living cartilaginous and bony fish, as well as the extinct placoderms and acanthodians. Tetrapods are descended from fish, so in a break from the long tradition of grouping all fish into a single class (Pisces), modern phylogenetics views fish as a paraphyletic group that includes all vertebrates except tetrapods. To treat fish as a monophyletic group, one would have to classify tetrapods as a clade/subgroup of specialized fish, which would make \"fish\" and \"vertebrates\" synonyms. In English, the plural of \"fish\" is fish when referring to individuals and fishes when referring to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg/500px-Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg/1280px-Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg/500px-Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Betta splendens, the Siamese fighting fish, is often referred to simply as a \"betta\" in the U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Betta_smaragdina_pair1.jpg/500px-Betta_smaragdina_pair1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Betta_smaragdina_pair1.jpg/500px-Betta_smaragdina_pair1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pair of Betta smaragdina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABetta_smaragdina_pair1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Betta_tussyae_%28male